modify-thresholds: fft_tbl array needs to be larger

This is the third patch required for "make tune-fft" to complete.

The read_table function reads the lines of tunefft.res
into the array fft_tbl. This array had a hardcoded size of 1000.

This is too small. For example,
on a Google Cloud c2 instance tunefft.res was 1597 lines long,
and on a c3 instance, it was 1033 lines long.

Buffer overflow causes modify-thresholds to crash,
and it fails to update gf2x/gf2x-thresholds.com

The simple-minded fix is just to increase the hardcoded size to 10000.

Apply from the gf2x source root with:  patch -p1 < this-file
---
--- a/src/modify-thresholds.c   2026-08-29 03:50:17.448052288 -0400
+++ b/src/modify-thresholds.c   2026-08-29 03:50:28.464054102 -0400
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
     int method;
 };

-struct fft_tuning_pair fft_tbl[1000];
+struct fft_tuning_pair fft_tbl[10000];
 unsigned long nstairs = 0;

 char * toom_info_string = "\"placeholder\"";
